# Dockerfile only COPYs apt-lists/ (build-environment config, ~20MB) --
# every actual build action (compiling uxplay_debug, running unit tests,
# etc.) bind-mounts its source via `docker run` instead. But the classic
# builder still hashes/tars the entire build context up front regardless
# of what the Dockerfile actually reads, so without this, every single
# `docker build .` (even one that's otherwise fully cache-hit) pays that
# cost against build/'s multi-GB scratch images -- pure wasted time on
# every build, not just the first one.
build/
golden-reference/
.git/
UxPlay/.git/
*.img
*.img.xz
